"""Two linked starter frames for the user-directed ejection sequence."""
import json
from pathlib import Path
OUT=Path(__file__).resolve().parent
PROJECT=OUT.parents[2]
LOCK='''ESCAPE SEQUENCE LOCK: Painted cinematic graphic-novel style matching the approved robot laboratory and escape doorway. Adult Harper has freckles, short curly auburn hair and hazel-green eyes; retain the same opaque silver halter top, modest framing and adult proportions. Headquarters is the original massive elongated dark graphite laboratory ark with tapering oval cyan culture galleries, amber longitudinal seams, asymmetric branching service spars and a restrained circular cyan aft drive. Escape pod is a DIFFERENT small enclosed one-person craft derived from its ivory-and-graphite boarding cabin: compact elongated ovoid hull, graphite structural ribs and seams, warm ivory cabin panels, one dark cushioned flight seat, cyan instruments, rounded boarding hatch, curved clear forward/side viewport and two small recessed cyan aft propulsion ports. No spherical bubble ship, biosphere domes or large external drive ring on the escape pod. Palette: graphite/ivory/cyan/amber, deep indigo-black cosmic background. Ship, cabin and pod design must remain coherent across views. No new characters, readable words, captions, watermark, panel divisions or collision-course solar framing.'''
interior='''Use case: illustration-story
Asset type: single 16:9 starter frame for an interior ejection shot, beginning at 1:19 and carrying through Leaving orbit at the moment. No text.
Inputs: Image1 is the approved bright boarding cabin from So bright: exact ivory panel finish, dark cushioned seat, cyan displays, rounded hatch and warm illumination. Image2 is Harper's adult face/silver laboratory costume identity. Image3 is the original graphite headquarters robot ship, for the hull visible through the pod window. These are design/identity references, not compositions to copy.
Primary request: We are INSIDE the one-person escape pod. A cinematic medium close/wide interior, camera just forward and to the right of the flight seat, looking diagonally back toward Harper on the LEFT side of frame. She sits firmly in the same dark cushioned seat from the boarding doorway, secured for launch by two ordinary wide padded graphite shoulder restraints attached to the seat and a subtle lap restraint below framing. Her freckled face, short curly auburn hair, silver halter and adult identity match Image2. Practical flight-safety framing, no sexual emphasis. Her hands rest low and are mostly below frame; do not feature fingers or fastening straps. She looks alert and resolved, glancing toward the SIDE WINDOW at right as release is about to occur.
The bright ivory cabin panels and cyan console wrap tightly around this single seat, matching Image1. A substantial curved rounded-rectangular side viewport fills the RIGHT half, showing the CLOSE original robot ship hull outside: graphite plating, amber seams, recognizable cyan culture gallery and a docking lip, with deep blue starfield beyond. The camera and Harper remain inside the pod; the mother ship is genuinely outside the glass. This is the starting instant just before the launch cradle lets go, so later video can make the hull and docking lip fall away through the window and reveal more stars. Depth separation is clear: cabin foreground, glass middle, external ark farther away. One modest amber latch-status accent gives a release cue, no readable labels.
Composition: Face/restraints and side-window view both readable at once. Warm cabin light and cool cyan hull reflection, rich illustrated texture, selective crisp panel lines, soft controlled bloom. Quiet dark bottom strip for lyrics. Do not copy the corridor view or draw a miniature pod inside a large room. Do not show the pod's exterior or a whole distant mother ship as an interior prop. No robot caregivers, water/tank, giant bubbles, new clothing or nude anatomy. Keep security visibly mechanical and practical rather than restraints with a fetish presentation.
'''+LOCK
exterior='''Use case: illustration-story
Asset type: single 16:9 EXTERIOR starter frame following the interior ejection, for Moments count here / Just perfect / We'll make all. No text.
Inputs: Image1 is the NEW interior escape-pod shot: authoritative one-seat ivory/graphite cabin, viewport, seat, scale and lighting. Reverse out a believable small enclosing hull around that cabin. Image2 is the original massive robot headquarters ship: preserve its complete graphite hull, cyan galleries, amber seams and service spars. Image3 is the earlier boarding doorway, reinforcing the small cabin and rounded hatch. This new pod is distinct from the spherical personal ship in the opening.
Primary request: The one-person pod has ALREADY been ejected safely clear of the robot ship. Camera outside in open space, showing a compact enclosed elongated ovoid capsule in the LOWER RIGHT foreground, about 20–24% frame width. It has ivory ceramic inset panels within dark graphite shell ribs, the same curved front/side cockpit viewport enclosing one seat, a flush rounded-rectangular SIDE boarding hatch, restrained amber seam lights, small cyan navigation accents and two recessed cyan aft ports. The cabin is small, integrated and plausible around the previous interior; through the tinted canopy the seat/warm ivory lighting may be barely visible, no giant detailed human face. No external giant ring or bubble shell.
The original headquarters ark is farther back across the LEFT and upper-middle, about 55–65% frame width, recognizably the same ship but not touching or overlapping the pod. Show clear depth and a substantial empty dark gap: the pod is several pod-lengths away from a small release recess in the ark's lower side. A restrained thin fading cyan-white ion/mist trail behind the pod curves back toward that release recess, showing where it came from. This is a functional ejection wake, not a laser beam, solid tether or luminous streak toward a sun. The wake is brightest just behind the pod and fades quickly toward the ship.
The pod initially points diagonally away from the hull toward lower-right OPEN SPACE. Leave ample empty right/upper-right starfield for a later bank and change of heading. Its nose, rear ports and escape direction are immediately legible. Painted indigo/violet distant nebulae, fine stars, warm/cool rimlight, rich material detail, quiet dark bottom lyric strip. The frame is the already-clear starting pose; later motion first extends the gap, then a brief bank/roll swings the pod's nose upward-right and it accelerates along a new arc. Do not depict the whole turn already completed or a long finished spaghetti trail.
Constraints: Exactly one mother ship and one small occupied escape capsule. Maintain the original ark proportions and the pod's coherent cabin-derived design. No additional ships, planets, sun, gigantic exhaust plume, spherical opening ship, missiles, explosion, debris, mother-ship roll or warp tunnel. Clear safe separation rather than a collision course. Full-frame illustration, not diagram or collage.
'''+LOCK
inputs_interior=[PROJECT/'generated/storyboard/escape-approach-v01/lab2-08.png',PROJECT/'generated/storyboard/lab-silver-v01/lab2-05.png',PROJECT/'generated/storyboard/lab-verse-v01/lab2-06.png']
inputs_exterior=[OUT/'escape-001.png',PROJECT/'generated/storyboard/lab-verse-v01/lab2-06.png',PROJECT/'generated/storyboard/escape-approach-v01/lab2-08.png']
records=[]
for sid,prompt,inputs in [('escape-001',interior,inputs_interior),('escape-002',exterior,inputs_exterior)]:
    (OUT/f'{sid}.prompt.txt').write_text(prompt,encoding='utf-8')
    records.append(dict(id=sid,prompt=prompt,inputs=[str(p) for p in inputs],destination=str(OUT/(sid+'.png')),
        itemId=sid+'-ejection-v01',status='pending generation'))
(OUT/'generation-input.json').write_text(json.dumps(dict(tool='built-in ImageGen',promptLock=LOCK,items=records),indent=2),encoding='utf-8')
print('Two dependency-linked starter-frame prompts prepared')
